.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt DEVFS 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm devfs
.Nd device file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm mount
.Fl t Cm devfs
.Cm devfs Ar node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the devices the kernel has, a node for each, under the name, owner, group and mode its
driver registered it with
.Pq Pa /dev/null , /dev/ttyv0 , /dev/pts/0 , /dev/gpt/rootfs .
The kernel mounts it on
.Pa /dev
at boot; it may be mounted elsewhere too
.Pq a Xr chroot 8 Ns 's Pa /dev ,
and each mount is a view of its own.
A device that appears gets a node in every view as soon as the view is looked at, and one that
goes loses its node.
.Pp
In a view, until it is unmounted
.Pq for Pa /dev , No until the system stops :
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Xr chmod 1 ,
.Xr chown 8
and
.Xr touch 1
change a node;
.It
removing a device's node hides that device in the view;
.It
directories and symbolic links can be made and removed.
.El
.Pp
Nothing else can be made:
regular files fail with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP ,
.Xr mknod 8
with
.Er EPERM ,
and hard links and renames with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.Pp
Every view has an empty directory
.Pa shm ,
mode 1777, where
.Xr fstab 5
mounts the
.Xr tmpfs 5
holding the POSIX shared memory objects of
.Xr shm_open 3 .
.Pp
A device node made with
.Xr mknod 8
on another file system opens the same device as the one here with its number.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /dev/shm -compact
.It Pa /dev
the
.Nm
mounted at boot
.It Pa /dev/shm
a
.Xr tmpfs 5 ,
from the default
.Xr fstab 5
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devfs.conf 5 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr tmpfs 5 ,
.Xr mount 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
appeared in FreeBSD 2.0.
In OxideBSD it was a part of oxfs until it became a file system type of its own in 0.3.0.
.Sh BUGS
FreeBSD's rulesets, which hide and show devices per view
.Pq Xr devfs 8 ,
aren't there yet.
